  <section id="get-started">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>How to Get Started with LoRa Mesh in Central PA</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        Getting on the Central PA Mesh is straightforward. Here's a basic path for most people to get started.
      </p>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>1. Get Hardware</h3>
          <p>A LoRa radio (Heltec, RAK, LilyGo, etc.) that supports Meshcore. Make sure it's the 915 MHz version for the US and Central Pennsylvania. See the <a href="#hardware">Hardware</a> section at the bottom of this page for common companion and repeater options.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>2. Flash Firmware</h3>
          <p>Use the official Meshcore web flasher or community tools. Most devices can be flashed in under a minute.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>3. Join the Network</h3>
          <p>Set the USA/Canada regional preset, power on, and start talking. Then hop into Discord to introduce yourself and find nearby nodes in Central PA.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section id="resources">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Resources for Meshcore & Meshtastic in Pennsylvania</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        Official and community links to help you get online and stay connected on the Central PA Mesh.
      </p>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Official Meshcore</h3>
          <p>
            <a href="https://meshcore.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">meshcore.io</a> · 
            <a href="https://flasher.meshcore.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">flasher.meshcore.io</a> · 
            <a href="https://map.meshcore.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">map.meshcore.io</a>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Getting Started</h3>
          <p>
            <a href="https://www.MeshcoreLearning.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.MeshcoreLearning.org</a> — A fantastic resource covering the basics of Meshcore and beyond.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Local Help</h3>
          <p>Ask in Discord for recommended frequencies, known repeaters, and people near you!</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="hardware">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Hardware</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        Companions are radios you use to chat. Standalone companions have a screen and a keyboard, joystick, or buttons, so you can read messages and type or send canned replies on the device itself, without a phone.
        App-connected companions talk over Bluetooth, USB, or Wi-Fi to the MeshCore or Meshtastic app on your phone or computer.
        Repeaters stay in one place, usually up high and often on solar, and pass messages along the mesh.
        This is only a sample of what’s available, not a complete list. Choose the 915&nbsp;MHz / US version for Central Pennsylvania. Some of these devices can also be bought on Amazon.
      </p>

      <div class="hw-group">
        <h3>Companions</h3>
        <p class="hw-lead">These are just a few picks; there are many more companion options available.</p>

        <h4 class="hw-sub">Standalone</h4>
        <p class="hw-lead">Type, read, and send on the device itself. A phone is optional, not required.</p>
        <div class="grid hw-grid">
          <article class="card hw-card">
            <img src="/images/hardware/lilygo-t-deck-plus.webp" width="800" height="600" alt="LilyGO T-Deck Plus handheld messenger with keyboard and color screen" />
            <div class="hw-card-body">
              <h3>LilyGO T-Deck Plus</h3>
              <span class="hw-fw">Both</span>
              <p>Handheld messenger with a keyboard, color screen, GPS, and a built-in battery. Type, read, and send on the device itself.</p>
              <p class="hw-sources"><span>Available from:</span> LilyGO, Rokland</p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="card hw-card">
            <img src="/images/hardware/wio-tracker-l1-pro.webp" width="800" height="600" alt="Seeed Wio Tracker L1 Pro handheld mesh radio with screen and antenna" />
            <div class="hw-card-body">
              <h3>Wio Tracker L1 Pro</h3>
              <span class="hw-fw">Both</span>
              <p>Compact handheld with a screen and joystick. Read messages, type on the on-screen keyboard, or send canned replies without a phone.</p>
              <p class="hw-sources"><span>Available from:</span> Seeed Studio, Rokland</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>

        <h4 class="hw-sub">App-connected</h4>
        <p class="hw-lead">Needs the MeshCore or Meshtastic app on your phone or computer, over Bluetooth, USB, or Wi-Fi.</p>
        <h5 class="hw-mini">Ready-made</h5>
        <div class="grid hw-grid">
          <article class="card hw-card">
            <img src="/images/hardware/sensecap-t1000-e.webp" width="800" height="600" alt="Seeed SenseCAP T1000-E credit-card sized pocket mesh tracker" />
            <div class="hw-card-body">
              <h3>SenseCAP T1000-E</h3>
              <span class="hw-fw">Both</span>
              <p>Credit-card-sized pocket tracker that pairs with your phone. IP65, with an internal antenna.</p>
              <p class="hw-sources"><span>Available from:</span> Seeed Studio, Rokland</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>

        <h5 class="hw-mini">DIY</h5>
        <div class="grid hw-grid">
          <article class="card hw-card">
            <img src="/images/hardware/heltec-wifi-lora-32-v3.webp" width="800" height="600" alt="Heltec WiFi LoRa 32 V3 development board in a clear case with antenna" />
            <div class="hw-card-body">
              <h3>Heltec WiFi LoRa 32 V3</h3>
              <span class="hw-fw">Both</span>
              <p>Popular, inexpensive ESP32-S3 board with an OLED. Add a battery, case, and antenna, then pair with the app.</p>
              <p class="hw-sources"><span>Available from:</span> Heltec, Rokland</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hw-group">
        <h3>Repeaters</h3>
        <p class="hw-lead">Fixed nodes that extend coverage. They don’t replace a phone or a handheld for chatting.</p>

        <h4>Ready-made</h4>
        <div class="grid hw-grid">
          <article class="card hw-card">
            <img src="/images/hardware/rak-wismesh-repeater.webp" width="800" height="600" alt="RAK WisMesh Repeater outdoor enclosure with solar panel and antenna" />
            <div class="hw-card-body">
              <h3>RAK WisMesh Repeater</h3>
              <span class="hw-fw">Both</span>
              <p>Ready-to-deploy outdoor solar repeater in an IP67 enclosure, with mounting hardware.</p>
              <p class="hw-sources"><span>Available from:</span> RAKwireless Store, Rokland</p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="card hw-card">
            <img src="/images/hardware/sensecap-solar-node-p1-pro.webp" width="800" height="600" alt="Seeed SenseCAP Solar Node P1-Pro with integrated solar panel" />
            <div class="hw-card-body">
              <h3>SenseCAP Solar Node P1-Pro</h3>
              <span class="hw-fw">Both</span>
              <p>All-in-one solar repeater with a 5&nbsp;W panel, batteries, GPS, and an external antenna.</p>
              <p class="hw-sources"><span>Available from:</span> Seeed Studio, Rokland</p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="card hw-card">
            <img src="/images/hardware/heltec-meshtower-v2.webp" width="800" height="600" alt="Heltec MeshTower V2 outdoor solar LoRa node on a stand" />
            <div class="hw-card-body">
              <h3>Heltec MeshTower V2</h3>
              <span class="hw-fw">Both</span>
              <p>Ready-made outdoor LoRa node with a solar panel, built for long-term installs.</p>
              <p class="hw-sources"><span>Available from:</span> Heltec, Rokland</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>

        <h4>DIY</h4>
        <div class="grid hw-grid">
          <article class="card hw-card">
            <img src="/images/hardware/rak-unify-solar-enclosure.webp" width="800" height="600" alt="RAK Unify solar enclosure for a DIY WisBlock repeater build" />
            <div class="hw-card-body">
              <h3>RAK4631 + solar enclosure</h3>
              <span class="hw-fw">Both</span>
              <p>Build your own solar repeater with a WisBlock board, Unify enclosure, battery, and panel.</p>
              <p class="hw-sources"><span>Available from:</span> RAKwireless Store, Rokland</p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="card hw-card">
            <img src="/images/hardware/heltec-t114-solar-kit.webp" width="800" height="600" alt="Heltec waterproof solar enclosure, front solar panel and open back with batteries and board" />
            <div class="hw-card-body">
              <h3>Heltec T114 + Solar Kit</h3>
              <span class="hw-fw">Both</span>
              <p>Low-power nRF52840 board plus Heltec’s waterproof solar enclosure and 18650 tray.</p>
              <p class="hw-sources"><span>Available from:</span> Heltec, Rokland</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hw-help">
        <p>
          Questions, or need help choosing and setting up a radio for MeshCore or Meshtastic?
          Visit our Discord or Facebook group — the community is happy to help.
        </p>
        <div class="cta-group">
          <a href="https://discord.gg/9wWs3Y7Cx5" class="icon-btn discord-btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="currentColor"><path d="M20.317 4.37a19.791 19.791 0 0 0-4.885-1.515.074.074 0 0 0-.079.037c-.21.375-.444.864-.608 1.25a18.27 18.27 0 0 0-5.487 0 12.64 12.64 0 0 0-.617-1.25.077.077 0 0 0-.079-.037A19.736 19.736 0 0 0 3.677 4.37a.07.07 0 0 0-.032.027C.533 9.046-.32 13.58.099 18.057a.082.082 0 0 0 .031.057 19.9 19.9 0 0 0 5.993 3.03.078.078 0 0 0 .084-.028 14.09 14.09 0 0 0 1.226-1.994.076.076 0 0 0-.041-.106 13.107 13.107 0 0 1-1.872-.892.077.077 0 0 1-.008-.128 10.2 10.2 0 0 0 .372-.292.074.074 0 0 1 .077-.01c3.928 1.793 8.18 1.793 12.062 0a.074.074 0 0 1 .078.01c.12.098.246.198.373.292a.077.077 0 0 1-.006.127 12.299 12.299 0 0 1-1.873.892.077.077 0 0 0-.041.107c.36.698.772 1.362 1.225 1.993a.076.076 0 0 0 .084.028 19.839 19.839 0 0 0 6.002-3.03.077.077 0 0 0 .032-.054c.5-5.177-.838-9.674-3.549-13.66a.061.061 0 0 0-.031-.03zM8.02 15.33c-1.183 0-2.157-1.085-2.157-2.419 0-1.333.956-2.419 2.157-2.419 1.21 0 2.176 1.096 2.157 2.42 0 1.333-.956 2.418-2.157 2.418zm7.975 0c-1.183 0-2.157-1.085-2.157-2.419 0-1.333.955-2.419 2.157-2.419 1.21 0 2.176 1.096 2.157 2.42 0 1.333-.946 2.418-2.157 2.418z"/></svg>
            Join Discord
          </a>
          <a href="https://www.facebook.com/share/g/1E1nHxfQyd/" class="icon-btn facebook-btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="currentColor"><path d="M24 12.073c0-6.627-5.373-12-12-12s-12 5.373-12 12c0 5.99 4.388 10.954 10.125 11.854v-8.385H7.078v-3.47h3.047V9.43c0-3.007 1.792-4.669 4.533-4.669 1.312 0 2.686.235 2.686.235v2.953H15.83c-1.491 0-1.956.925-1.956 1.874v2.25h3.328l-.532 3.47h-2.796v8.385C19.612 23.027 24 18.062 24 12.073z"/></svg>
            Join Facebook
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <div class="container">
      <img src="/logo.jpg" alt="Central PA Mesh" class="footer-logo" />
      <p>
        Central PA Mesh · CPAMe.sh<br>
        Decentralized Communities · LoRa Mesh Networking in Central Pennsylvania
